  "details": "Hello,\nI have issues receiving invites, invite requests and friend requests as well as an issue which occurred with a recent patch where my social list wont update, but let me explain those two issues in more detail.\nFirst lets talk about the social list that wont update. This issue first occurred with the release of VRChat 2020.4.1, build number 1004.\nFor this I did some testing: I joined a friend into a public instance while he was there and left after. I rejoined about 30 min later, arriving in an empty instance. I loaded back into my homeworld, then to another instance and then joined on him again to see if it did update (took me about 5 min) and it didnt, loading me into an empty instance. Since he is in my favorites, I checked if there was a difference between favorites and online friends, but found none. I left VRChat about 2h later (still with him displaying online in the same public instance) checking the social list on the webpage, where it said that he is in fact offline for about 2 hours.\nThis issue is recreatable with alot of my friends, but it does not seem to be consistent as sometime only a few friends update, but I was unable to determine an exact condition when and why.\nAs of now the only way to fix this issue is to restart VRChat.\nThen there is the issue about not receiving invites, invite requests and friend requests. This one I have for more than a year and I cant tell when it started. Usually this isnt a big issue for me, but I thought mentioning this one aswell wouldnt hurt. The conditions for this one are approximately 30 min playtime and/or loading into 3 more instances. The effect is me not receiving any notifications as mentioned. Opening the browser and logging into the VRChat homepage shows all notifications, which dont show ingame. This issue can also be recreated anytime and is affecting every social notification.\nAs of now the only way to fix this issue is to restart VRChat.\nTo fix these issues I tried to reinstall VRChat, clear the cache, reinstall Steam and logging into a different VRChat account to see if the problems is tied to my account (they are not).\nI live in the EU, my ping to the VRChat servers are at a stable 190ms with no connection issues.\nIf you require more data/testing, I can provide you with everything you need.\nKind regards,\nLazar",
